{%- comment -%}
  A body paragraph under a heading, as a block.

  **Named for what it is, not for where it first appeared.** The class was
  `.lookbook__intro` — the theme's one lede, but named after the single section
  that happened to own it. It is `.section-lede` now, and the lookbook uses that
  too, so a second caller does not have to choose between an odd class name and
  forking the numbers.

  Carries default text for the reason the subheading does: a block that renders
  nothing until it is filled in is invisible the moment it is added, with no
  element for the editor to select, which reads as a broken block rather than
  an empty one.
{%- endcomment -%}


{%- liquid
  assign align_class = ''
  if block.settings.alignment != blank and block.settings.alignment != 'inherit'
    assign align_class = ' align-' | append: block.settings.alignment
  endif

  comment
    A guard rather than interpolating whatever is stored: an unknown value would
    print as a tag name and Liquid would emit `<foo>`. Same shape as the level
    guard on `blocks/title.liquid`.
  endcomment
  assign tags = 'span,p,h1,h2,h3,h4,h5,h6' | split: ','
  assign tag = 'p'
  if tags contains block.settings.element
    assign tag = block.settings.element
  endif
-%}
{%- if block.settings.text != blank -%}
  <{{ tag }}
    class="section-lede reveal{{ align_class }}"
    style="{% render 'block-spacing', padding: block.settings.padding %}{% render 'text-style', preset: block.settings.style, font_style: block.settings.override_font, font_size: block.settings.override_size, color: block.settings.color, line_height: block.settings.override_leading, text_case: block.settings.override_case, letter_spacing: block.settings.override_tracking %}"
    {{ block.shopify_attributes }}
  >{{ block.settings.text }}</{{ tag }}>
{%- endif -%}

